[In response to the discussion about whether it is "fair" for the monsters
to get cheap shots at an adventurer with an AC of -38]

Well, certainly we don't want characters ever able to just walk the dungeon
ignoring every monster in sight, but it should be good enough to keep a
healthy level of abject terror in the player's mind if being offed by a single
blow happened _occassionally_.  How about taking out the damage lessening
code, leaving in the distribution of AC's between -1 and current highly
negative class, but making that something more favorable than a linear
distribution; perhaps that rne distribution would work.

If the game doesn't stay nearly impossible to win, you'll soon all be
working on new varieties of fiendishness for Nethack 4.0, to keep the
rif-raf out of the high score table, exactly the same thing that motivated
this release.  ;-)

There should be some characters it is to all appearances and experiences
_impossible_ to win with, so that when someone finally does, s/he has
something to really crow about.  Else, what's a score table for?

